Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:14:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: ask encri to unlock at startup, and stop if the vault
 stays shut

The spike's Gecko asks for the profile's secret at startup and waited
up to 10 seconds for the vault, then started with the profile's keys
locked. On the user's word (encriox W15), a browser with its vault
locked brings up encri's unlock instead, and does not go on without it.

EncriUnlock shows encri's own screens, letting the browser in and
unlocking the vault as each is needed, from whichever of the browser's
activities is in the foreground, or the next one to come there. Gecko's
startup and the gate share one request and wait on the same answer. If
the vault is still shut once the screens are done, or does not answer
in 30 seconds, the browser finishes its activities, leaves the recent
apps and ends its process, before Gecko has opened anything of the
profile. The gate's `kek withhold` still starts Gecko locked, to measure
what Gecko does then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
